Changelog: 19-11-2026 11:02:34

Fixed. Test 29 is called Display Session, DisplayPort and HDMI (owner, 19-11-2026), the same name as in the
PS5's Board Test; it was Display Session. Its description names the connector status it already shows. The
wiki's tables have the new name.

Changelog: 19-11-2026 09:14:46

Release 4.0.0.

Changelog: 19-11-2026 04:48:47

Breaking. Test 53 (Wi-Fi Adapter) no longer checks BC-250 Wi-Fi Adapter's service, built modules and loaded
driver: the app is no longer part of the suite (owner, 19-11-2026). The test still lists every Wi-Fi adapter and
whether the kernel has a driver and firmware for it. For an AIC8800D80 stick it now says that Bazzite's kernel has
no driver for it.

Changelog: 18-11-2026 20:42:52

Release 3.2.1.

Changelog: 18-11-2026 19:03:02

Fixed. Test 28, Suspend Targets, no longer says that resume from sleep is broken and no longer asks for the sleep
targets to be masked (owner, 18-11-2026, after two sleeps on a board with BIOS P5.00 and kernel 7.3.4, which both
came back). It now reports what is there: the sleep states the kernel offers, whether systemd may use them, and the
good and failed suspends since boot. Where suspend-to-idle is the only sleep, it says what that means on this board:
the screen goes to no signal, the board stays powered with its fan running and draws about as much as awake, and the
power button wakes it. A failed suspend since boot is a warning. Unmasked sleep targets are no warning anymore. The
test's line in the app and in the wiki say the same.

